{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793000706,"nonce":"JDejCmHahanyyBJ7cTfY4A7ftR0=","title":"Use the browser client's keyboard conventions in editing controls","message":"RayDE correctly detects the browser visitor's platform, but ashui TextEditing, CodeFind, CodeEditor modifier-click navigation and menu editing dispatch read Sys.systemName(). WASM reports its runtime platform, so Cmd+A/C/V, find/replace and Cmd+click on a Mac browser use the wrong modifier. Provide one optional application keyboard-platform override shared by these controls, preserve native defaults, and validate both Mac and Windows/Linux browser input. RayDE supplies its detected visitor platform before UI construction.","files":null}]}